<section class="w-full bg-surface-container-low px-margin md:px-margin-desktop py-16 shadow-inner">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto flex flex-col gap-space-lg">
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center text-center gap-space-xs">
            <span class="font-label-sm text-label-sm text-optic-disc-gold uppercase tracking-widest">Scientific
                Clarifications</span>
            <h2 class="font-headline-lg text-headline-lg text-text-primary">Clinical &amp; Technical FAQ</h2>
            <p class="font-body-md text-body-md text-text-secondary max-w-xl">
                Key protocols regarding offline edge deployment, regulatory positioning, camera interoperability, and
                anatomical generalization.
            </p>
        </div>
        <!-- Accordion Container -->
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-space-sm" id="faqAccordion">
            <!-- Accordion Item 1 -->
            <div class="rounded-xl bg-surface-container overflow-hidden shadow-sm transition-all duration-200">
                <button aria-expanded="false"
                    class="faq-toggle w-full p-space-md text-left flex items-center justify-between gap-space-sm hover:bg-surface-bright/40 transition-colors"
                    type="button">
                    <span class="font-title-md text-title-md text-text-primary flex items-center gap-2.5">
                        <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-optic-disc-gold text-[20px]">lan</span>
                        Can FundusGuard AI operate within an air-gapped hospital network without cloud connectivity?
                    </span>
                    <span
                        class="material-symbols-outlined text-[20px] text-text-secondary faq-icon transition-transform duration-200">expand_more</span>
                </button>
                <div class="faq-content max-h-0 overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out px-space-md">
                    <div
                        class="pb-space-md font-body-sm text-body-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed border-t border-surface-bright/40 pt-space-sm">
                        Yes. While a cloud-assisted REST API is accessible for testing, the core SPI-OWL neural pipeline
                        is
                        compiled to ONNX runtime format and Docker containers specifically engineered for local edge
                        workstation deployment. When running on local hardware (standard CPU or workstation GPU), fundus
                        photographs never leave your clinic’s firewall, ensuring absolute patient data confinement and
                        zero
                        external transmission.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <!-- Accordion Item 2 -->
            <div class="rounded-xl bg-surface-container overflow-hidden shadow-sm transition-all duration-200">
                <button aria-expanded="false"
                    class="faq-toggle w-full p-space-md text-left flex items-center justify-between gap-space-sm hover:bg-surface-bright/40 transition-colors"
                    type="button">
                    <span class="font-title-md text-title-md text-text-primary flex items-center gap-2.5">
                        <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-optic-disc-gold text-[20px]">photo_camera</span>
                        What fundus camera models and image specifications are supported?
                    </span>
                    <span
                        class="material-symbols-outlined text-[20px] text-text-secondary faq-icon transition-transform duration-200">expand_more</span>
                </button>
                <div class="faq-content max-h-0 overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out px-space-md">
                    <div
                        class="pb-space-md font-body-sm text-body-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed border-t border-surface-bright/40 pt-space-sm">
                        The preprocessing module accepts standard color fundus photography (CFP) centered on the optic
                        nerve
                        head (ONH) or macula. File ingestion includes native DICOM (.dcm), uncompressed 16-bit TIFF,
                        PNG,
                        and standard JPEG. Calibrations have been verified across Topcon (TRC series), Zeiss (Visucam,
                        Clarus), Canon (CR-2 AF), Centervue (DRSplus), and smartphone-based indirect adapters with
                        appropriate optical focal centering.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <!-- Accordion Item 3 -->
            <div class="rounded-xl bg-surface-container overflow-hidden shadow-sm transition-all duration-200">
                <button aria-expanded="false"
                    class="faq-toggle w-full p-space-md text-left flex items-center justify-between gap-space-sm hover:bg-surface-bright/40 transition-colors"
                    type="button">
                    <span class="font-title-md text-title-md text-text-primary flex items-center gap-2.5">
                        <span
                            class="material-symbols-outlined text-optic-disc-gold text-[20px]">health_and_safety</span>
                        Is FundusGuard AI an FDA / CE-IVD approved diagnostic medical device?
                    </span>
                    <span
                        class="material-symbols-outlined text-[20px] text-text-secondary faq-icon transition-transform duration-200">expand_more</span>
                </button>
                <div class="faq-content max-h-0 overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out px-space-md">
                    <div
                        class="pb-space-md font-body-sm text-body-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed border-t border-surface-bright/40 pt-space-sm">
                        No. FundusGuard AI and the SPI-OWL engine are currently classified as Investigational
                        Decision-Support Prototypes designed solely for clinical research, retrospective validation
                        studies,
                        and academic triage workflows. It does not replace comprehensive slit-lamp biomicroscopy,
                        Humphrey
                        visual field perimetry, or licensed physician clinical judgment. Autonomous prescription or
                        unsupervised primary diagnosis is strictly disallowed.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <!-- Accordion Item 4 -->
            <div class="rounded-xl bg-surface-container overflow-hidden shadow-sm transition-all duration-200">
                <button aria-expanded="false"
                    class="faq-toggle w-full p-space-md text-left flex items-center justify-between gap-space-sm hover:bg-surface-bright/40 transition-colors"
                    type="button">
                    <span class="font-title-md text-title-md text-text-primary flex items-center gap-2.5">
                        <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-optic-disc-gold text-[20px]">public</span>
                        How does the research team account for ethnic &amp; anatomical variations in cup morphology?
                    </span>
                    <span
                        class="material-symbols-outlined text-[20px] text-text-secondary faq-icon transition-transform duration-200">expand_more</span>
                </button>
                <div class="faq-content max-h-0 overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out px-space-md">
                    <div
                        class="pb-space-md font-body-sm text-body-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed border-t border-surface-bright/40 pt-space-sm">
                        Normal physiological cupping varies widely across ethnic cohorts (e.g., higher average disc
                        diameters and physiological CDRs in African-descent cohorts vs. Caucasian and East Asian
                        populations). To prevent over-referral bias, our validation datasets incorporate multi-source
                        public
                        and institutional databases (including RIM-ONE, REFUGE, ORIGA, and local South Asian clinical
                        records), specifically adjusting neuroretinal rim boundary confidence weights for myopic tilt
                        and
                        peripapillary atrophy (PPA).
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <!-- Consultation Scheduling Ribbon -->
        <div
            class="p-space-lg rounded-xl bg-gradient-to-r from-surface-container to-surface-container-high flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-space-md shadow-md">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-space-sm">
                <div
                    class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-primary-container/20 flex items-center justify-center text-primary-container shrink-0">
                    <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[28px]">video_camera_front</span>
                </div>
                <div class="flex flex-col">
                    <h3 class="font-title-md text-title-md text-text-primary">Need a Structured Technical Video
                        Consultation?</h3>
                    <p class="font-body-sm text-body-sm text-text-secondary">We schedule 30-minute academic walkthroughs
                        with university departments and clinical trial sponsors.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <a class="shrink-0 px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg bg-surface-container-highest hover:bg-surface-bright text-on-surface font-label-md text-label-md transition-colors flex items-center gap-2"
                href="mailto:clinical@fundusguard.ai?subject=Request%20for%20Clinical%20Walkthrough">
                <span>Arrange Video Briefing</span>
                <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[16px]">arrow_forward</span>
            </a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
<script src="../assets/scripts/faq.js" nonce="<%= nonce %>"></script>